<!--
  The breaking-change inventory for this package. Generated, never hand-written
  (dotnet pack -p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true), which also drops this comment and writes
  CRLF, so both are restored afterwards. Ten entries:

  CP0002 x1 PaginateConfigBuilder.WithGuards: its four parameters became int? so that naming one
  guard stops silently resetting the other three to the engine constants. Source-compatible,
  binary-breaking, and the only signature change in the set.

  CP0014 x9, one shape: a member that used to be compiler-generated is hand-written now, so an
  attribute the compiler had put there is gone. PaginateLinkContext and PaginateFilterFieldMetadata
  hand-write Equals/GetHashCode because the synthesized versions compare a collection member by
  reference; PaginateLikeDefaults.set_Strategy gained a null guard; PaginateComposedQuery.SortBy went
  back to non-nullable when the tie-breaker became mandatory at Build().

  Two of those nine are the newest and are this change's own: declaring PaginateLinkContext's two
  positional properties takes CompilerGeneratedAttribute off their init accessors. That declaration
  IS the fix — a guard held in a field initializer is skipped by `with`, because a record's copy
  constructor copies fields verbatim, and an init accessor is the only place that runs on both paths.

  Most of them are visible only because the ApiCompat attribute rule is now on: nullable context and
  CompilerGeneratedAttribute live in metadata the signature comparison does not read, so they would
  have shipped silently before.

  Delete this file when PackageValidationBaselineVersion moves past 10.0.3: every entry exists only
  against that baseline, and a stale suppression hides the next accidental break behind it.
-->
